WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.566
This converter runs entirely in your browser,

2
00:00:02.682 --> 00:00:05.294
so the file you paste never leaves your machine.

3
00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.872
Here is a customer list with the two things

4
00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:10.449
that break most converters — an address with

5
00:00:10.484 --> 00:00:11.923
a comma inside quotes,

6
00:00:12.098 --> 00:00:14.257
and a Boston ZIP code that starts with a

7
00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:17.752
zero. Paste it in and the JSON appears straight

8
00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:20.144
away. Look at the table preview.

9
00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:22.419
The quoted name stayed one field,

10
00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:24.532
and the ZIP kept its leading zero,

11
00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:26.761
because a cell only becomes a number when it

12
00:00:26.796 --> 00:00:29.304
can be written back as exactly the same text.

13
00:00:29.547 --> 00:00:31.927
Turn type inference off and every value comes

14
00:00:31.974 --> 00:00:33.472
back as a string instead.

15
00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:36.061
Switch direction and it works the other way

16
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.439
too. Nested objects flatten to dot notation,

17
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:40.972
arrays are serialised,

18
00:00:41.146 --> 00:00:42.678
and every key gets a column.

19
00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:45.674
Rows with the wrong number of fields are reported

20
00:00:45.709 --> 00:00:47.903
with their line numbers rather than quietly

21
00:00:47.973 --> 00:00:49.911
mangled. Then copy it,

22
00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:52.547
or download the file. No upload,

23
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:55.031
no signup, nothing stored anywhere.
